        <headline>Beach Hazards Statement issued September 26 at 2:08PM PDT until September 28 at 5:00AM PDT by NWS San Diego CA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Beach Hazards Statement, minor tidal overflow
expected due to the combination of high tides and elevated surf.
For the Coastal Flood Advisory, minor coastal flooding expected
due to the combination of high tides and elevated surf.

* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County
Coastal Areas.

* WHEN...For the Beach Hazards Statement, through late Sunday
night. For the Coastal Flood Advisory, from 5 AM Monday to 5
PM PDT Wednesday.

* IMPACTS...Minor coastal flooding and minor coastal erosion
expected during high tides. Additionally, elevated surf will
lead to strong rip currents.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Elevated surf of 3-5 feet expected. Local
sets to 6 feet possible on south-facing beaches. Morning high
tides are expected to peak between 6.7 feet and 7.0 through
Wednesday, peaking Tuesday morning. The listed tide predictions
have been corrected to reflect current trends in actual tide
observations.
</description>
        <instruction>Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous swimming conditions.
Avoid beaches during morning high tides.</instruction>
